  "articleBody": "Trying to do a DIY roof inspection is tempting, but there are some common pitfalls that can lead to missed issues or even make things worse. Texas weather is no joke, and our roofs take a beating. Just because you don't see obvious damage from the ground doesn't mean your roof is in the clear. Many significant problems can be subtle or in hard-to-see areas. Avoiding these common mistakes can save you a lot of grief and money down the road, ensuring your roof actually gets the thorough check it needs without putting yourself at risk or creating new problems. It's about being smart and safe with your biggest home protector.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\n1. Walking on a damaged or steep roof: This is super dangerous! You could fall, or you could cause more damage to already weakened areas. Always prioritize safety. If it's too steep or looks damaged, call a pro.\n2. Assuming no ground-visible damage means no issues: Many critical problems like loosened flashing, soft spots, or hidden hail impacts aren't obvious from the ground. Professional inspections often uncover these.\n3. Treating caulk as a permanent fix: Caulk and sealants are temporary solutions at best. They aren't meant to be long-term repairs for serious roof issues and can often mask bigger problems that need proper attention.\n4. Ignoring your attic or drainage system: Your roof isn't just the shingles. Problems in your attic (like moisture) or with your gutters (like excessive granules) are major indicators of roof health. Always check these areas.\n5. Delaying repairs after an issue is identified: Even a small problem can quickly escalate into a major, costly repair when exposed to Texas's harsh weather. Prompt action after discovering an issue is crucial. Discounted Roofing Co. can help you assess any issues and get them fixed quickly and correctly, protecting your home for years to come.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}